Dtimsstart: the selection help in two messages.

Message 33 of Dtimsstart.tmsg, the input method selection help, is over
the 1024 bytes a System V catalogue message may hold (NL_TEXTMAX), and
gencat refuses the file. The text is now messages 33 and 35, and the
resource line names both; the merged app-defaults file is byte-identical
to before.

--- a/programs/dtimsstart/Dtimsstart	2026-11-20 12:03:13
+++ b/programs/dtimsstart/Dtimsstart	2026-11-20 12:03:13
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@
 Dtimsstart*Mode*cmd_rc.marginWidth:	%|nls-32-#20#|
 
 ! help message
-Dtimsstart.selectionHelpMsg:	%|nls-33-#Input method selection help#|
+Dtimsstart.selectionHelpMsg:	%|nls-33-#Input method selection help#|%|nls-35-##|
 
 Dtimsstart.modeHelpMsg:	%|nls-34-#IM Selection mode help#|
 
--- a/programs/localized/C/app-defaults/Dtimsstart.tmsg	2026-11-20 12:03:13
+++ b/programs/localized/C/app-defaults/Dtimsstart.tmsg	2026-11-20 12:03:13
@@ -136,8 +136,9 @@
 \\n \
       [Cancel]:    discards the selection and closes the window.\\n \
 \\n \
-      [Help]:      shows this message.\\n \
-\\n \\n \
+      [Help]:      shows this message.\\n
+$ the rest of message 33: one message over 1024 bytes is refused
+35  \\n \\n \
        NOTE:  input methods not installed on the system will be listed\\n \
               with netted, and cannot be selected.\\n \
 \\n \
